(Plan 290 regression: a text-variable source appended into a
fixed-size buffer must still honor the bounds check - the same
truncate-and-set-error behavior a literal/format-string source already
has (see tests/067_format_buffer_fixed_overflow.vox). A gap here would
be a memory-safety regression, not a cosmetic one - the analyzer fix
must not bypass _buffer_append_bytes's clamp for this newly-accepted
source kind.)

a buffer called dst is 8 bytes in size.
a text called payload is "1234567890".

append payload to dst.
print dst.
on error print "append overflow".

clear dst.
a text called fits is "1234567".
append fits to dst.
print dst.
on error print "should not overflow".
